- **Sanitize User Input**: Before processing the email content, sanitize it to prevent injection attacks. Remove or escape any potentially harmful characters. Example:
  ```javascript
  const sanitizedContent = emailContent.replace(/[\r\n]+/g, ' ').trim();
  ```

- **Strict Keyword Matching**: Ensure that the keywords for unsubscribe requests are strictly matched and not just checked for presence. This can prevent false positives from unrelated content. Example:
  ```javascript
  const unsubscribe = this.unsubscribeKeywords.some(keyword => 
    new RegExp(`\\b${keyword}\\b`, 'i').test(emailContent)
  );
